## Frequently Asked Questions

### Q: Does it work with a pattern lock, PIN and password?
A: Yes. CrookCatcher reacts to a wrong PIN, pattern or password. Failed fingerprint or face unlock attempts don't trigger it, and it doesn't work with pop-up cameras.

### Q: Will the person know they were photographed?
A: CrookCatcher works in the background without showing a camera preview. On Android 13 and newer, Android shows a small indicator while the camera is in use, which is a system feature apps can't hide.

### Q: Do I need an account?
A: No. There's no registration. You only connect a Gmail account if you want alert emails.

### Q: Who can see my photos?
A: Only you. Alerts are sent from your own Gmail account, and the developer never sees your photos. Read more in the [privacy policy](/privacy).

### Q: Does it drain the battery?
A: No. CrookCatcher only activates when an unlock attempt fails, so battery usage is minimal.

### Q: Is there an iPhone version?
A: No. iPhones don't allow apps to detect failed unlock attempts, so CrookCatcher is available for Android only.

### Q: Does it work after restarting my phone?
A: Yes, after you unlock your phone once following a restart. Until then, Android doesn't allow apps to react to unlock attempts.

